  render_theorem(sec7b, "Channel Independence Theorem (VERIFIED)", "Coupling class prediction of 2000 elements from Z/214,414,200: mod-8 channel alone (8 bins) achieves 67.9% accuracy. mod-9 alone (9 bins) achieves 49.9% (= baseline). mod-8 + mod-9 combined (72 bins) achieves 84.5%. Eigenvalue sum (200 bins) achieves 51.4% -- barely above random (50.2%). Information grows multiplicatively with channel count. Summing destroys it.");
  render_p(sec7b, "The mod-9 channel achieves exactly the baseline because it is orthogonal to parity: whether n is even or odd is invisible in n mod 9. But combined with mod-8, mod-9 further separates the odd elements by divisibility by 3. This is CRT in action: independent channels carry independent information.");
