  render_theorem(sec7e, "Projection Forgetting Theorem (VERIFIED)", "Two tasks with different per-channel transition patterns (strides differ in all 7 channels of Z/214,414,200). Per-channel bigram tables. Full overwrite: 0% retention (catastrophic forgetting). Projector (mod-8 from task B, 6 channels from task A): 85.7% retention = 6/7 exactly. Algebraic guarantee from CRT channel independence.");
  render_p(sec7e, "The sacrifice is optimal: mod-8 is the coarsest channel (only 8 possible residues). It carries the least fine-grained information and is the fastest to relearn. The 6 preserved channels (mod-9 through mod-17) carry the finer structure that is expensive to learn and critical to retain.");
