  render_p(sec7i, "The curriculum penalty grows with channels: Z/210 17/7=2.43x, Z/12,612,600 115/49=2.35x, Z/214,414,200 132/49=2.69x. Simultaneous training outperforms ALL curricula. Chain order = real algebra (group-theoretic decomposition), NOT trainable capability phases. Channel independence is so strong that each channel converges at its intrinsic q_i-step rate regardless of what other channels are doing.");
